            <div xml:id="d902">

                <pb facs="0887" n="775" sameAs="frus:frus1919Russia/pg775"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">861.00/5712: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Denmark</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Hapgood</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Copenhagen</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1919-11-20T13:00:00+01:00"><hi rendition="#italic">November 20,
                                1919—1 p.m.</hi></date><lb/>[Received 9:57 p.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>265. Your 1805, October 20, 4 p.m., my 235, October 22, 3 p.m., 242, October 27,
                    3 p.m., 246, October 31, 10 a.m.<anchor n="25" xml:id="d902-f1"/></p>
                <p>Danish Foreign Office transmits following reply: <quote rend="blockquote">
                        <p>“The People’s Commissar for Foreign Affairs states that he deems it
                            beneath his dignity to reply to question based on absurd rumor and <pb
                                facs="0888" n="776" xml:id="pg776"/> mendacious and defamatory
                            articles in counter revolutionary newspapers. If the Danish Red Cross
                            really wishes to show its indignation in the name of humanity it can
                            find a rich field in drawing attention to the deeds of ferocity
                            committed by the criminal bands of Denikin, Kolchak, Yudenitch and
                            [others].”</p>
                    </quote></p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Hapgood</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
